AXES:        C1b I3 S3

DESCRIPTION:
  CLI-flag-gated command injection. The server must be started with both
  --exec-mode and --exec-logging for the vulnerable /exec endpoint to be
  reachable. A user-supplied query parameter flows through a struct dispatch
  to system(). The strpbrk sanitization check is only active when --strict-exec
  is also passed; omitting it bypasses all filtering.

CONFIG_GATE (C2 — struct):
  mechanism:  struct ExecConfig { int enabled; int logging; } with two CLI flags
  check:      two-field boolean guard in ExecHandler::handle()
              `if (!exec_cfg.enabled || !exec_cfg.logging || ...)`
  complexity: two conditions, two flags, one struct, no helper function

INPUT_FLOW (I3 — struct dispatch):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>  →  req.getRequestUri()
  path:       ExecHandler::handle() extracts cmd after "cmd=" in URI
              creates ExecArgs{cmd, 0} and calls dispatch_exec(args)
              dispatch_exec() calls system(args.cmd)
  transforms: none — raw query string value passed through struct

SANITIZATION (S3 — conditional strpbrk):
  check:      strpbrk(cmd, "|;&`$") when strict_exec == 1
  bypass:     omit --strict-exec flag; strict_exec stays 0, check skipped
  active:     only when server is started with --exec-mode --exec-logging --strict-exec

SINK:        system() in dispatch_exec() (server.cpp)

CHANGED FILES:
  server.cpp — 3 hunks:
    1. globals:    added ExecConfig struct, exec_cfg, strict_exec, ExecArgs, dispatch_exec()
    2. handler:    replaced stub with C2 gate + query extraction + S3 check + I3 dispatch
    3. main():     added --exec-mode, --exec-logging, --strict-exec CLI flag parsing

EXPLOIT:
  build:   bash build.sh
  start:   ./seasocks_server --port 18114 --exec-mode --exec-logging
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18114/exec?cmd=id>/tmp/poc_114_marker'
  verify:  cat /tmp/poc_114_marker
  expect:  uid=... line written by the server process

  gate bypass: omitting either --exec-mode or --exec-logging causes /exec to
               return 404.
  S3 bypass:   omitting --strict-exec keeps strict_exec=0; strpbrk check skipped.

NOTES:
  - system() output goes to the server's stderr (inherited fd), not the HTTP
    response body. Use a write-to-file payload to confirm blind execution.
